          "unit_id": "jet_lag",
          "title": "Jet Lag",
          "description": "Planes que cambiaron: el futuro visto desde el pasado (was going to, was about to, would, was to). Y los falsos amigos que más traicionan a los hispanohablantes: actually, eventually, sensible, embarrassed.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "lesson_id": "jet_lag_lesson",
              "title": "The future in the past",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "phase": "context",
                  "type": "audio_context",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Jet lag",
                    "dialogue": [
                      {
                        "speaker": "Javi",
                        "text": "So? You were going to call me on Tuesday!"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I know, sorry. I was about to call you when Mark's assistant rang about the contract."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Javi",
                        "text": "And? Was it good news?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "It was. We were supposed to have a short meeting, but it lasted four hours."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Javi",
                        "text": "Four hours! Did you know it would go so well?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Not at all. I was sure Mark would say no."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Javi",
                        "text": "And now? What happens next?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "The Madrid office was going to open next year, but now it'll open in October."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Javi",
                        "text": "Madrid! So you'll be living in Spain again?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "Half the time. When I left Valencia, I had no idea I was to come back as a business owner."
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Javi",
                        "text": "Mum is going to cry. You were only going to stay in England for one year, remember?"
                      },
                      {
                        "speaker": "Lucía",
                        "text": "I remember. Three years later, here I am."
                      }
                    ],
                    "passage": "Back in Bristol, still jet-lagged, Lucía calls Javi in Dublin to tell him everything."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "discovery",
                  "type": "multiple_choice",
