                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "The future in the past",
                    "explanation": "Para hablar del futuro desde un punto del pasado:\n• was / were going to: plan del pasado, a menudo no cumplido. You were going to call me on Tuesday!\n• was about to: a punto de. I was about to call you when…\n• would: futuro visto desde el pasado. I was sure Mark would say no.\n• was / were supposed to: lo previsto, que no se cumplió. We were supposed to have a short meeting.\n• was to (narrativo y formal): lo que iba a ocurrir después, como si fuera el destino. I had no idea I was to come back as a business owner.\n• was due to: estaba programado.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Forma",
                        "Uso",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "was / were going to",
                          "plan que no se cumplió",
                          "You were going to call me on Tuesday!"
                        ],
                        [
                          "was about to",
                          "a punto de",
                          "I was about to call you when…"
                        ],
                        [
                          "would",
                          "futuro visto desde el pasado",
                          "I was sure Mark would say no."
                        ],
                        [
                          "was / were supposed to",
                          "lo previsto (y no fue así)",
                          "We were supposed to have a short meeting."
                        ],
                        [
                          "was to (narrativo)",
                          "lo que el destino tenía preparado",
                          "I had no idea I was to come back as a business owner."
                        ],
                        [
                          "was due to",
                          "estaba programado",
                          "The office was due to open next year."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "You were going to call me on Tuesday!",
                      "I was about to call you when Mark's assistant rang.",
                      "We were supposed to have a short meeting, but it lasted four hours.",
                      "You were only going to stay in England for one year."
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "False friends: actually, eventually, sensible, embarrassed",
                    "explanation": "Los falsos amigos se parecen a una palabra española pero significan otra cosa. A nivel C1 se espera no confundirlos:\n• actually = en realidad (no «actualmente», que es currently / at the moment).\n• eventually = finalmente, al final (no «eventualmente»).\n• sensible = sensato (sensible en español es sensitive).\n• embarrassed = avergonzado (embarazada es pregnant).\n• assist = ayudar (asistir a algo es attend).\n• library = biblioteca (librería es bookshop).\n• carpet = moqueta, alfombra (carpeta es folder).\n• realise = darse cuenta (realizar es carry out / do).\n• constipated = estreñido (constipado es have a cold).\n• argument = discusión, pelea; también argumento de una tesis (el argumento de una película es plot).\n• exit = salida (éxito es success).",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Inglés",
                        "Significa",
                        "Para decir…",
                        "…se usa"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "actually",
                          "en realidad",
                          "actualmente",
                          "currently"
                        ],
                        [
                          "eventually",
                          "al final",
                          "eventualmente",
                          "possibly, if necessary"
                        ],
                        [
                          "sensible",
                          "sensato",
                          "sensible",
                          "sensitive"
                        ],
                        [
                          "embarrassed",
                          "avergonzado",
                          "embarazada",
                          "pregnant"
                        ],
                        [
                          "attend",
                          "asistir",
                          "ayudar",
                          "assist / help"
                        ],
                        [
                          "library",
                          "biblioteca",
                          "librería",
                          "bookshop"
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "I'm not tired. Actually, I feel great.",
                      "The meeting lasted four hours, but eventually Mark said yes.",
                      "Opening in Madrid first is a sensible decision.",
                      "I was so embarrassed when I forgot to call Javi."
                    ]
                  }
